<%= l_ui_title_bar(
  title: "Combobox",
  breadcrumbs: [
    ["Home", root_path]
  ]
) %>

<p class="mt-4">A token select: a text input with type-ahead filtering whose selections become removable <%= link_to "tags", tags_path %>, in the style of an email recipient field. It is built on the ARIA combobox pattern - the input carries <code>role="combobox"</code> and points at the highlighted option with <code>aria-activedescendant</code>, so focus stays in the input while the list is browsed - and needs no third-party select library.</p>

<p class="mt-4">Each selection carries its own hidden input, so the control submits with an ordinary form post. A blank value is always posted first, so clearing every token submits an empty collection rather than omitting the parameter and leaving the association untouched.</p>

<h2 class="mt-8 l-ui-heading--section">Multi select</h2>

<p class="mt-4">The default. Type to filter, choose with Enter or a click, and remove a token with its ✕ or by pressing Backspace on the empty input. Choosing an option that is already selected removes it again.</p>

<div class="l-ui-form mt-4">
  <%= l_ui_combobox("message[recipient_ids]",
        label: "Recipients",
        collection: @recipients,
        selected: @recipients.first(2).map(&:last),
        placeholder: "Add a recipient",
        hint: "Search by email address.") %>
</div>

<div class="mt-6" data-controller="l-ui--modal">
  <button class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--outline l-ui-button--small" data-action="l-ui--modal#open">View code</button>
  <dialog class="l-ui-modal" data-l-ui--modal-target="dialog" data-action="click->l-ui--modal#closeOnBackdrop" aria-labelledby="modal-combobox-multi-heading">
    <div class="l-ui-modal__header">
      <h3 id="modal-combobox-multi-heading">Multi select</h3>
      <button class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--icon" data-action="l-ui--modal#close" aria-label="Close">
        <%= image_tag "layered_ui/icon_close.svg", alt: "", class: "l-ui-icon l-ui-icon--sm", aria: { hidden: true } %>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class="l-ui-modal__body">
      <pre class="l-ui-surface"><code>&lt;%= l_ui_combobox("message[recipient_ids]",
      label: "Recipients",
      collection: User.pluck(:email, :id),
      selected: @message.recipient_ids,
      placeholder: "Add a recipient",
      hint: "Search by email address.") %&gt;

# message[recipient_ids][] => ["", "3", "7"]</code></pre>
    </div>
  </dialog>
</div>

<h2 class="mt-8 l-ui-heading--section">Single select</h2>

<p class="mt-4">Pass <code>multiple: false</code> for a one-of-many control. The parameter loses its <code>[]</code> suffix, choosing an option replaces the current token, and the listbox closes on selection. Use it where a <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> would be unwieldy because the list is long.</p>

<div class="l-ui-form mt-4">
  <%= l_ui_combobox("message[owner_id]",
        label: "Owner",
        collection: @recipients,
        multiple: false,
        placeholder: "Choose an owner") %>
</div>

<div class="mt-6" data-controller="l-ui--modal">
  <button class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--outline l-ui-button--small" data-action="l-ui--modal#open">View code</button>
  <dialog class="l-ui-modal" data-l-ui--modal-target="dialog" data-action="click->l-ui--modal#closeOnBackdrop" aria-labelledby="modal-combobox-single-heading">
    <div class="l-ui-modal__header">
      <h3 id="modal-combobox-single-heading">Single select</h3>
      <button class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--icon" data-action="l-ui--modal#close" aria-label="Close">
        <%= image_tag "layered_ui/icon_close.svg", alt: "", class: "l-ui-icon l-ui-icon--sm", aria: { hidden: true } %>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class="l-ui-modal__body">
      <pre class="l-ui-surface"><code>&lt;%= l_ui_combobox("message[owner_id]",
      label: "Owner",
      collection: User.pluck(:email, :id),
      multiple: false,
      placeholder: "Choose an owner") %&gt;

# message[owner_id] => "7"</code></pre>
    </div>
  </dialog>
</div>

<h2 class="mt-8 l-ui-heading--section">Remote options</h2>

<p class="mt-4">Pass <code>url:</code> and the options are fetched from that endpoint as the user types, rather than being rendered up front and filtered in the browser - for collections too large to send with the page. Requests are debounced, and a response that has been overtaken by a later one is discarded, so the list always answers what is currently typed. <code>min_chars:</code> sets how much has to be typed before the first search runs; it defaults to <code>0</code>, which searches as soon as the field is focused.</p>

<p class="mt-4">The endpoint is sent <code>term</code> and <code>page</code> and answers with JSON. Include <code>Layered::Ui::ComboboxOptions</code> in the controller and <code>l_ui_combobox_options</code> builds that payload: it searches with Ransack and pages with Pagy when they are available, and falls back to a plain <code>LIKE</code> with <code>limit</code>/<code>offset</code> when they are not, so neither gem is required. Matches come a page at a time: reaching the end of the list appends the next page, whether the end is reached by scrolling to it or by pressing the down arrow on the last option, so the keyboard is never capped at the first page. Until the list is complete, the note under the options says how far into the matches it has got. A request in flight is a spinner rather than a message - at the trailing edge of the field while searching, beside the note while a further page loads - and it only appears once a request has been running long enough to be worth reporting, so a quick answer never flashes one. The endpoint stays an ordinary action in your own app, so it is scoped and authorised exactly as any other index is.</p>

<p class="mt-4">Because the browser holds no copy of the collection, a selected value cannot be looked up for its label, so pass remote selections as <code>[label, value]</code> pairs, as the owner field below does.</p>

<p class="mt-4">Every string the control can show is in <code>text:</code>, so it can be reworded or translated where it is used - <code>empty:</code>, <code>create:</code>, <code>min_chars:</code>, <code>progress:</code>, <code>error:</code> and <code>more_error:</code>. Placeholders use Rails' own <code>%{name}</code> syntax: <code>%{term}</code> for the value being created, <code>%{count}</code> for the character threshold, and <code>%{shown}</code> with <code>%{count}</code> for the progress line. Pass <code>progress: nil</code> to drop the progress line altogether. The recipients field below is reworded; the owner field keeps the defaults.</p>

<div class="l-ui-form mt-4">
  <%= l_ui_combobox("message[recipient_ids]",
        label: "Recipients",
        url: combobox_options_path,
        min_chars: 2,
        text: {
          empty: "Nobody by that name",
          progress: "%{shown} of %{count} people. Keep typing to narrow the list.",
          min_chars: "Type %{count} letters to start searching."
        },
        placeholder: "Search for a person",
        hint: "Search by name or email address. There are #{User.count} people to choose from.") %>

  <div class="mt-4">
    <%= l_ui_combobox("message[owner_id]",
          label: "Owner",
          url: combobox_options_path,
          multiple: false,
          selected: @owner_selection,
          placeholder: "Search for a person") %>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="mt-6" data-controller="l-ui--modal">
  <button class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--outline l-ui-button--small" data-action="l-ui--modal#open">View code</button>
  <dialog class="l-ui-modal" data-l-ui--modal-target="dialog" data-action="click->l-ui--modal#closeOnBackdrop" aria-labelledby="modal-combobox-remote-heading">
    <div class="l-ui-modal__header">
      <h3 id="modal-combobox-remote-heading">Remote options</h3>
      <button class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--icon" data-action="l-ui--modal#close" aria-label="Close">
        <%= image_tag "layered_ui/icon_close.svg", alt: "", class: "l-ui-icon l-ui-icon--sm", aria: { hidden: true } %>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class="l-ui-modal__body">
      <pre class="l-ui-surface"><code>&lt;%= l_ui_combobox(:recipient_ids, form: f,
      label: "Recipients",
      url: options_users_path,
      min_chars: 2,
      text: {
        empty: "Nobody by that name",
        progress: "%{shown} of %{count} people. Keep typing to narrow the list.",
        min_chars: "Type %{count} letters to start searching."
      },
      placeholder: "Search for a person") %&gt;

&lt;%= l_ui_combobox(:owner_id, form: f,
      label: "Owner",
      url: options_users_path,
      multiple: false,
      selected: [[@message.owner.name, @message.owner_id]]) %&gt;

# config/routes.rb
resources :users do
  get "options", on: :collection
end

# app/controllers/users_controller.rb
class UsersController &lt; ApplicationController
  include Layered::Ui::ComboboxOptions

  def options
    render json: l_ui_combobox_options(User.all, label: :name, search: [:name, :email])
  end
end

# GET /users/options?term=ali
{ "options": [{ "label": "Alice Johnson", "value": "2" }],
  "page": 1, "pages": 1, "count": 1 }</code></pre>
    </div>
  </dialog>
</div>

<h2 class="mt-8 l-ui-heading--section">Creating new values</h2>

<p class="mt-4">With <code>create: true</code>, a term that matches no option is offered as a new token. New values post under their own parameter (<code>create_name:</code>, which is then required), so the server never has to guess whether a submitted value is an existing record's ID or a free-text label. On redisplay, pass previously created values in <code>selected:</code> alongside the existing ones - any selected value that is not in the collection is rendered as a new token.</p>

<div class="l-ui-form mt-4">
  <%= l_ui_combobox("post[tag_ids]",
        label: "Tags",
        collection: [["Announcement", "1"], ["Release", "2"], ["Tutorial", "3"]],
        selected: ["1", "backstage"],
        create: true,
        create_name: "post[new_tag_names]",
        placeholder: "Add a tag",
        hint: "Type a tag that doesn't exist yet to add it.") %>
</div>

<div class="mt-6" data-controller="l-ui--modal">
  <button class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--outline l-ui-button--small" data-action="l-ui--modal#open">View code</button>
  <dialog class="l-ui-modal" data-l-ui--modal-target="dialog" data-action="click->l-ui--modal#closeOnBackdrop" aria-labelledby="modal-combobox-create-heading">
    <div class="l-ui-modal__header">
      <h3 id="modal-combobox-create-heading">Creating new values</h3>
      <button class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--icon" data-action="l-ui--modal#close" aria-label="Close">
        <%= image_tag "layered_ui/icon_close.svg", alt: "", class: "l-ui-icon l-ui-icon--sm", aria: { hidden: true } %>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class="l-ui-modal__body">
      <pre class="l-ui-surface"><code>&lt;%= l_ui_combobox(:tag_ids, form: f,
      label: "Tags",
      collection: Tag.pluck(:name, :id),
      selected: @post.tag_ids + @post.new_tag_names.to_a,
      create: true,
      create_name: :new_tag_names) %&gt;

# post[tag_ids][]       => ["", "1"]
# post[new_tag_names][] => ["backstage"]

# app/controllers/posts_controller.rb
tags  = Tag.where(id: params[:post][:tag_ids])
tags += Array(params[:post][:new_tag_names]).map { |name| Tag.find_or_create_by!(name:) }
@post.tags = tags</code></pre>
    </div>
  </dialog>
</div>

<h2 class="mt-8 l-ui-heading--section">Reordering tokens</h2>

<p class="mt-4">With <code>reorder: true</code> each token gains a pair of move controls plus a grip handle, and tokens can be dragged with a mouse. The grip is decorative (<code>aria-hidden</code>) - it exists so the drag is discoverable rather than hidden, and the token takes a grab cursor to match. Parameters post in the order shown, so the field can express a ranking. The move buttons are not decoration: dragging on its own would fail WCAG 2.2 SC 2.5.7, which requires a single-pointer alternative - and they are the only way to reorder on a touch screen. Reordering is off by default, since most fields treat their selections as a set.</p>

<div class="l-ui-form mt-4">
  <%= l_ui_combobox("survey[choice_ids]",
        label: "Preferences, most wanted first",
        collection: [["Dark mode", "1"], ["Offline support", "2"], ["Keyboard shortcuts", "3"], ["Export to CSV", "4"]],
        selected: %w[1 2 3],
        reorder: true,
        placeholder: "Add a preference") %>
</div>

<div class="mt-6" data-controller="l-ui--modal">
  <button class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--outline l-ui-button--small" data-action="l-ui--modal#open">View code</button>
  <dialog class="l-ui-modal" data-l-ui--modal-target="dialog" data-action="click->l-ui--modal#closeOnBackdrop" aria-labelledby="modal-combobox-reorder-heading">
    <div class="l-ui-modal__header">
      <h3 id="modal-combobox-reorder-heading">Reordering tokens</h3>
      <button class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--icon" data-action="l-ui--modal#close" aria-label="Close">
        <%= image_tag "layered_ui/icon_close.svg", alt: "", class: "l-ui-icon l-ui-icon--sm", aria: { hidden: true } %>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class="l-ui-modal__body">
      <pre class="l-ui-surface"><code>&lt;%= l_ui_combobox("survey[choice_ids]",
      label: "Preferences, most wanted first",
      collection: Choice.pluck(:name, :id),
      selected: @survey.choice_ids,
      reorder: true) %&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
  </dialog>
</div>

<h2 class="mt-8 l-ui-heading--section">Inside a form builder</h2>

<p class="mt-4">Pass the attribute as a Symbol with <code>form:</code> and the parameter names are derived from the builder, exactly as they would be for a built-in field helper.</p>

<div class="mt-4">
  <%= form_with url: "#", method: :post, scope: :post, class: "l-ui-form" do |f| %>
    <%= l_ui_combobox(:tag_ids, form: f,
          label: "Tags",
          collection: [["Announcement", "1"], ["Release", "2"], ["Tutorial", "3"]],
          placeholder: "Add a tag") %>

    <div class="l-ui-form__actions">
      <button type="submit" class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--primary">Save</button>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>

<div class="mt-6" data-controller="l-ui--modal">
  <button class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--outline l-ui-button--small" data-action="l-ui--modal#open">View code</button>
  <dialog class="l-ui-modal" data-l-ui--modal-target="dialog" data-action="click->l-ui--modal#closeOnBackdrop" aria-labelledby="modal-combobox-builder-heading">
    <div class="l-ui-modal__header">
      <h3 id="modal-combobox-builder-heading">Inside a form builder</h3>
      <button class="l-ui-button l-ui-button--icon" data-action="l-ui--modal#close" aria-label="Close">
        <%= image_tag "layered_ui/icon_close.svg", alt: "", class: "l-ui-icon l-ui-icon--sm", aria: { hidden: true } %>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class="l-ui-modal__body">
      <pre class="l-ui-surface"><code>&lt;%= form_with model: @post do |f| %&gt;
  &lt;%= l_ui_combobox(:tag_ids, form: f,
        label: "Tags",
        collection: Tag.pluck(:name, :id),
        selected: @post.tag_ids) %&gt;
&lt;% end %&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
  </dialog>
</div>

<h2 class="mt-8 l-ui-heading--section">Disabled</h2>

<p class="mt-4">Pass <code>disabled: true</code> to disable the input and every token control. The selections still post, so a disabled combobox does not silently clear the field.</p>

<div class="l-ui-form mt-4">
  <%= l_ui_combobox("message[recipient_ids]",
        label: "Recipients",
        collection: @recipients,
        selected: @recipients.first(1).map(&:last),
        disabled: true) %>
</div>

<h2 class="mt-8 l-ui-heading--section">Keyboard</h2>

<div class="l-ui-table-container mt-4">
  <table class="l-ui-table">
    <caption class="l-ui-sr-only">Combobox keyboard interactions</caption>

    <thead class="l-ui-table__header">
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__header-cell" scope="col">Key</th>
        <th class="l-ui-table__header-cell" scope="col">Action</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>

    <tbody class="l-ui-table__body">
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row">Down / Up</th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Open the list, entering it from the first (Down) or last (Up) visible option, then move the highlight through the options, wrapping at each end</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row">Home / End</th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Highlight the first or last visible option</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row">Enter</th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Choose the highlighted option, or add it as a new value in create mode. With nothing highlighted, Enter is left to the form</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row">Escape</th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Close the list, or clear the typed term when it is already closed</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row">Backspace</th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Remove the last token when the input is empty</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row">Tab</th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Close the list and move on to the next control</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
